## Why This Is Asked
This question probes testing of a real-time, multi-tenant streaming system with shared infrastructure (Kafka, MongoDB). It tests end-to-end latency, exactly-once processing, tenant isolation, privacy-focused test data, and canary-based deployment practices.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end latency (p95/p99)
- Exactly-once semantics and deduping
- Tenant isolation on shared resources
- Data privacy and redaction in tests
- Canary deployments and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Dedup logic in consumer
let seen = new Set();
while ((ev = nextEvent()) !== null) {
  if (seen.has(ev.id)) continue;
  seen.add(ev.id);
  process(ev);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure latency under spike and set alert thresholds?
- How would you rollback a failing canary without affecting tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for live schema migrations and canary rollouts are critical in scalable services. This question probes practical techniques for migration tests, compatibility guarantees, and safe rollback.

## Key Concepts

- In-place schema migrations, backward/forward compatibility, feature flag gating, canary deployment, cross-region data consistency, rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Migration test scaffold (pseudo)
async function testMigration(seed, migrate, verify){
  await seed(0);
  await migrate(1);
  await verify(1);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you simulate partial migration across regions and measure impact?
- What metrics trigger rollback and what tooling helps ensure rollback correctness?

